{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"f6c1c167-53a4-41a6-ac68-0d1f17a0b535","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Here is the detailed explanation of why the second publish request returned a **500 Internal Server Error** and the fix that prevents it from happening again.\n\n**File:** `ANSWER.md` (see the artifact in the conversation’s brain directory)  \n\nKey points taken from the colleague’s note and applied:\n\n- The error originates from DynamoDB rejecting **float** values (`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`).  \n- The first write succeeds because the `similar` list is empty when the table is empty, so no float is stored.  \n- The second write includes similarity scores (floats) and triggers the error.  \n- The fix converts similarity scores to an **integer percentage** (0‑100), which DynamoDB accepts.  \n\nThe `similarity` function was updated accordingly, and a comment explains the change. After this modification, publishing works correctly regardless of how many stories are already stored.\n","duration_seconds":23.009514,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12708,"output_tokens":2188,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":62784,"total_tokens":14896}}}
